{"title":"Topicwise Test-24 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Electromagnetic Fields-2","fileName":"083_Topicwise Test-24 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Electromagnetic Fields-2.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider a magnetic flux density <img src=\"/media/a593e8868d97c28433cda3f556279c2ee8facfef.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 0.01sin377t Wb/m<sup>2</sup>. The emf induced about the circular path of radius, <em>r</em> = 0.5 m, z = 0 at t = 0 due to B is _______ .</p>\n<p>\n (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-3","high":"-2.9"},"solution":"<p>\n -2.96 (-3.00 - -2.90)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c8811e27c579a5614fdf127117aa9a75ef6a6cad.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A wire of non magnetic material with radius ‘<em>R</em>’ and length <img src=\"/media/e3b57c89502e9bfee8e71b564dcbb37a89f87a74.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> carries a current <img src=\"/media/125182301fa84c29fcb1c484452b5c6c27ee7cae.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> which is uniformly distributed over the its cross-section. The magnetic field energy inside the wire will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/e62d08c312aa88ed2582e79db48ad97423931d44.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/63801951d336cac6ac563ecb2cc8054318516ffb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/73a77aa7618e2b4411f279eae194992a72f75c33.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0531036ce059cf462ccaa370ea89485c67